# The depot: Lamplight clocked in. The tune is stiff, in E minor, and counted in sevens
# (2+2+3), so it never quite settles. The punch clock is in the drums.
# For eight bars the beat relaxes to 4/4 and the real tune gets out in G major.
# The eighth note never changes speed, so the machine can grab it straight back.
tempo 208
meter 7/8
grid 7
key E minor
form Clock A A2 Free Back

